ts, and swung the lead from -11.4 to +10.7 for Black. The engine wanted G3. Black had just captured at A9 and left a ko point at B9, and this move did not make use of it."}, {"turn": 67, "text": "Ahead by +10.1, Opus 5.5 played F2 and the lead dropped to -11.8, a loss of 21.9 points. The engine preferred J2. It was the worst of Black's two blunders, and it handed back the whole advantage in one move."}, {"turn": 68, "text": "The 14k answered with G1, which lost 21.9 points and sent the lead from -11.8 back to +10.1, with J5 as the engine's choice. Black's win was restored on the very next move, and after that the lead stayed between +9.8 and +10.2 until the passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "count.py only flood-fills the pasted board to count stones and enclosed territory (with optional dead stones removed), and libs.py only lists each group's stones and liberties and flags those with two or fewer; both work on the current position and neither generates, scores or ranks moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}